# SMART Health Check-in 1.0 outline dependency tree

Source outline: `spec.md.outline`

Purpose: organize expansion so canonical text for prerequisite sections is
completed before dependent sections are drafted canonically. Drafts within a
tranche can run in parallel, but a tranche should not be marked complete until
its organizer has reconciled cross-references, conformance rules, examples, and
schema/vector implications.

## Ground rules for expansion

- Treat each numbered section or subsection listed below as an expansion unit.
- For each unit, run five independent draft attempts, then have an organizer
  synthesize one canonical section.
- The organizer output for every normative unit should include:
  - final Markdown prose for the section;
  - one-row-per-rule conformance inventory for Appendix A;
  - cross-reference updates needed elsewhere;
  - JSON Schema / CDDL / fixture implications, if any;
  - unresolved questions, only if the section cannot be completed safely.
- Do not canonicalize a dependent unit until all listed prerequisite units are
  canonical.
- Active protocol facts to preserve throughout:
  - the clinical request/response model is transport-neutral;
  - the same-device direct `org-iso-mdoc` flow is the base presentation flow;
  - the kiosk flow wraps the same-device flow and re-enters it on the phone;
  - kiosk request payloads embed the SMART request directly, not demo preset
    wrappers;
  - `profilesFrom` is an array of canonical profile-family URLs;
  - `profiles` plus `profilesFrom` are additive selectors, not narrowing
    selectors.

