## Parallel drafting batches

Recommended batch boundaries for the five-draft/organizer workflow:

1. Batch T1.A: editorial conventions, terminology, references.
2. Batch T1.B/T1.C: purpose, scope, architecture, roles, flows.
3. Batch T2.A: request model and selectors.
4. Batch T2.B: response model and validation.
5. Batch T2.C/T2.D: FHIR mapping and JSON Schema.
6. Batch T3.A: trust framework.
7. Batch T3.B: same-device direct mdoc flow.
8. Batch T3.C/T3.D: SessionTranscript, CDDL, byte ladders, ISO notes.
9. Batch T4.A/T4.B: kiosk request, pointer, phone resolution.
10. Batch T4.C/T4.D: kiosk submission, desktop completion, kiosk fixtures.
11. Batch T5.A/T5.D/T5.F: conformance, registries, checklist.
12. Batch T5.B/T5.C/T5.E: security, privacy, internationalization.
13. Batch T6.A: implementation notes.
14. Batch T6.B/T6.C: examples and fixture index.
15. Batch T7: OID4VP placeholder, future work, final matter.

Each batch should produce an organizer note listing any upstream text that must
be reopened. Reopenings should be exceptional; if a downstream batch discovers a
real contradiction, pause the next tranche and patch the prerequisite section
before continuing.
